  "result": "Fixed. The command now prints `27.06`.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py:9` padded the fractional part on the wrong side. `\"12.5\"` became `\"5\".rjust(2, \"0\")` \u2192 `\"05\"`, which reads as 12.05 instead of 12.50. That gives 1205 \u00d7 2 = 2410, plus 8.25% tax (199) = 26.09, which is the wrong output you saw. The fraction needs zeros added on the right, so I changed `rjust` to `ljust`. The correct sum is 2500 + 206 tax = 27.06.\n\nI also checked `to_cents` directly: `12` \u2192 1200, `12.5` \u2192 1250, `12.05` \u2192 1205, `0.5` \u2192 50 and `12.` \u2192 1200.\n\n**Tests:** pytest isn't installed, so I ran `python3 -m unittest`. All 6 tests pass. None of them test `to_cents` with a one-digit fraction, which is why this slipped through. I can add a regression test in `tests/` if you'd like.",
